From 532d0fa92e34305c545cdddb6b27ff1e0638051d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:38:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] fix(post): write a sub-micrometre short arc as a feed on
 the stream lattice

After the re-read of #3471: the app posts through cnc::serialize, which
writes whole micrometres. A generator arc with a chord under 1 um (a
0.09 um fillet, #3463) rounded to a record whose end equals its start,
the stream's full-turn form, and every post wrote a full circle (a
G02 of R50 through the part in the new app test). The writer now knows
the true start (cnc_arc_lattice.rs) and writes such an arc, when its
true sweep is half a turn or less, as a Feed to its rounded end. A
near-full turn and a stated full turn keep their arc record.

The 1e-5 mm band of the previous commit is dropped: a full turn is a
record with equal ends or a sweep over half a turn, never ends that
are only close. tinyg's band is reverted; heidenhain's chord path reads
equal ends as a full turn.

Pinned by cnc_arc_lattice.rs (post) and short_arc_lattice.rs (app:
whole job, per operation, per mount, mm and inch), the rule test, and
the rotary case on Fanuc and Doosan.

Refs #3442
Refs #3463

